                  <items count="7">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Pick a site on a satellite map: search an address or place (Nominatim / Photon, OpenStreetMap data), click or drag the pin, then "Use this location". The map window stays in front of Rhino and Grasshopper while it is open. Latitude and Longitude (WGS84 degrees) go into LiDAR Site, Site Context or any component that takes a site. The pick is saved with the document. Imagery: Esri World Imagery; map: © OpenStreetMap contributors. Needs an internet connection.

Version 1.19.0.827</item>
